'\"
.TH "rbc::MARKER" 3tcl 0\&.5\&.0 "rbc" "Upgraded Tcl/Tk9\&.0-ready RBC package"
.SH NAME
rbc::MARKER - Commands in namespace rbc::MARKER
.SH "GRAPH MARKER MARKER COMMAND"
.PP
Commands in this namespace document graph markers\&.
.PP
MARKER is used below as a placeholder for:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
GRAPHINST marker
.fi
.RE
.PP
Markers are graph annotations\&. They are independent of graph elements and do not contribute to the calculation
of axis limits\&.
.PP
Rbc provides six marker types:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Type| Description
_
bitmap| Displays a Tk bitmap
image| Displays a Tk image
line| Displays one or more connected line segments
polygon | Displays a filled and/or outlined polygon
text| Displays text
window| Displays an embedded Tk window
.TE
.PP
A marker is created by specifying its type:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
graph \&.g
\&.g marker create text -name label -coords {1\&.0 2\&.0} -text "Operating point"
\&.g marker create line -name limit -coords {0 5 10 5} -outline red
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unlike elements and pens, the marker name is not a positional argument of MARKER create\&. Use -name to
select an explicit name\&. If -name is omitted, Rbc generates a marker name\&.
.SH "MARKER COORDINATES"
.PP
Marker coordinates are graph coordinates and are mapped through the axes selected by -mapx and -mapy\&.
.PP
The number of coordinates depends on the marker type:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Marker type | Coordinates
_
bitmap| One or two X-Y pairs
image| One X-Y pair
line| Two or more X-Y pairs
polygon| Three or more X-Y pairs
text| One X-Y pair
window| One X-Y pair
.TE
.PP
An empty -coords value leaves the marker without drawable coordinates\&.
.PP
Markers may also use -Inf and Inf coordinates\&. These track the minimum and maximum limits of the
corresponding axis\&. This is useful for annotations that must remain attached to an edge of the plotting area\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -coords {-Inf Inf} -anchor nw -text "upper left"
.fi
.RE
.SH "DRAWING ORDER"
.PP
Markers have their own display order\&. MARKER before and MARKER after change the position of a marker in
that order\&.
.PP
By default markers are drawn over graph elements\&. The -under option changes whether an individual marker is
drawn below or above the element layer\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker configure region -under yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
The marker ordering operations affect ordering between markers; they do not replace the -under setting\&.
.SH "ELEMENT ASSOCIATION"
.PP
-element associates a marker with an element:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -name note -element signal -coords {2 5} -text signal
.fi
.RE
.PP
The marker is displayed only while the associated element is displayed\&. An empty -element value removes the
association\&.
.SH "MARKER BINDINGS"
.PP
Markers participate in graph component bindings\&. Bindings are made with MARKER bind\&.
.PP
Every marker has its marker name as an implicit binding tag\&. Additional tags are selected with -bindtags\&.
.PP
The default binding tags depend on the marker type:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Type| Default -bindtags
_
bitmap| Bitmap all
image| Image all
line| Line all
polygon | Polygon all
text| Text all
window| Window all
.TE
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -name note -coords {1 2} -text "click me" -bindtags {annotation all}
\&.g marker bind annotation <Button-1> {
    puts "annotation selected"
}
.fi
.RE
.SH "MARKER TYPES AND OPTIONS"
.PP
All marker types share the coordinate, visibility, axis-mapping, naming, binding, state, drawing-order, and
offset options described below\&. Each concrete marker type then adds its own drawing options\&.
.PP
MARKER cget and MARKER configure operate on the option table of the concrete marker being addressed\&. An
option valid for one marker type is not necessarily valid for another\&.
.SS "COMMON MARKER OPTIONS"
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-bindtags tagList| Specifies additional binding tags associated with the marker\&. The marker name is always an implicit binding tag\&. The default class tag depends on the marker type\&.
-coords coordList| Specifies the graph coordinates of the marker\&. The required number of coordinates depends on the marker type\&. The default is empty\&.
-element elementName | Associates the marker with an element\&. The marker is displayed only while that element is displayed\&. An empty value removes the association\&.
-hide boolean| Specifies whether the marker is hidden\&. The default is no\&.
-mapx axisName| Specifies the X axis used to map marker coordinates\&. The default is x\&.
-mapy axisName| Specifies the Y axis used to map marker coordinates\&. The default is y\&.
-name markerName| Specifies the marker name\&. When omitted during creation, Rbc generates a name\&.
-state state| Specifies the marker state\&. The default is normal\&.
-under boolean| Specifies whether the marker is drawn below graph elements rather than above them\&. The default is no\&.
-xoffset distance| Adds a horizontal screen-coordinate offset after the marker has been mapped\&. The default is 0\&.
-yoffset distance| Adds a vertical screen-coordinate offset after the marker has been mapped\&. The default is 0\&.
.TE
.SS "BITMAP MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Bitmap markers display a Tk bitmap\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create bitmap -name bitmap1 -coords {1 2} -bitmap questhead
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, bitmap markers support:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-anchor anchor| Specifies how the bitmap is positioned relative to its reference coordinates\&. The default is center\&.
-background color | Specifies the bitmap background color\&. This is a synonym for -fill\&.
-bg color| Synonym for -background\&.
-bitmap bitmap| Specifies the Tk bitmap to display\&.
-fill color| Specifies the bitmap background color\&.
-foreground color | Specifies the bitmap foreground color\&. This is a synonym for -outline\&.
-fg color| Synonym for -foreground\&.
-mask bitmap| Specifies an optional bitmap mask\&.
-outline color| Specifies the bitmap foreground color\&.
-rotate degrees| Specifies the rotation angle in degrees\&. The default is 0\&.
.TE
.SS "IMAGE MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Image markers display a Tk image\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
image create photo icon -file icon\&.png
\&.g marker create image -name iconMarker -coords {1 2} -image icon
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, image markers support:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-anchor anchor| Specifies how the image is positioned relative to its coordinate\&. The default is center\&.
-image imageName | Specifies the Tk image to display\&.
.TE
.SS "LINE MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Line markers draw connected line segments through their X-Y coordinate pairs\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create line -name threshold -coords {-Inf 5 Inf 5} -outline red -linewidth 2
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, line markers support:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-cap style| Specifies the line cap style\&. Accepted styles are butt, projecting, and round\&. The default is butt\&.
-dashes dashList| Specifies the dash pattern\&. An empty value selects a solid line\&.
-dashoffset distance | Specifies the offset into the dash pattern\&. The default is 0\&.
-fill color| Specifies the secondary line color\&. An empty value disables the secondary color\&.
-join style| Specifies how adjacent segments are joined\&. Accepted styles are bevel, miter, and round\&. The default is miter\&.
-linewidth distance| Specifies the line width\&. The default is 1\&.
-outline color| Specifies the primary line color\&. The default is black\&.
-xor boolean| Specifies whether the line is drawn using XOR drawing\&. The default is no\&.
.TE
.SS "POLYGON MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Polygon markers draw the closed polygon formed by their coordinate pairs\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create polygon -name region -coords {0 0 4 0 4 3 0 3} -fill lightblue -outline navy
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, polygon markers support:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-dashes dashList| Specifies the dash pattern used for the polygon outline\&. An empty value selects a solid outline\&.
-fill color| Specifies the polygon fill color\&. An empty value makes the interior transparent\&.
-linewidth distance | Specifies the width of the polygon outline\&.
-outline color| Specifies the color of the polygon outline\&.
-stipple bitmap| Specifies an optional stipple bitmap used when filling the polygon\&. An empty value selects a solid fill\&.
.TE
.SS "TEXT MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Text markers display one or more lines of text\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
\&.g marker create text -name annotation -coords {3 8} -text "maximum" -anchor s
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, text markers support:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-anchor anchor| Specifies how the text is positioned relative to its coordinate\&. The default is center\&.
-background color | Specifies the text background color\&. This is a synonym for -fill\&.
-bg color| Synonym for -background\&.
-fill color| Specifies the text background color\&.
-font font| Specifies the font used to draw the text\&.
-foreground color | Specifies the text color\&. This is a synonym for -outline\&.
-fg color| Synonym for -foreground\&.
-justify justify| Specifies justification of multiline text\&. The default is left\&.
-outline color| Specifies the text color\&. The default is black\&.
-padx padding| Specifies horizontal padding around the text\&. The default is 4\&.
-pady padding| Specifies vertical padding around the text\&. The default is 4\&.
-rotate degrees| Specifies the text rotation angle in degrees\&. The default is 0\&.
-shadow shadow| Specifies the text shadow\&.
-text text| Specifies the text to display\&.
.TE
.SS "WINDOW MARKER OPTIONS"
.PP
Window markers display a Tk window inside the graph\&.
.PP
The window must be managed by the graph marker\&.
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
button \&.g\&.info -text Info
\&.g marker create window -name infoMarker -coords {2 4} -window \&.g\&.info
.fi
.RE
.PP
In addition to the common marker options, window markers support:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Option| Description
_
-anchor anchor| Specifies how the window is positioned relative to its coordinate\&. The default is center\&.
-height distance | Specifies an explicit height for the embedded window\&. A value of 0 uses its requested height\&.
-width distance| Specifies an explicit width for the embedded window\&. A value of 0 uses its requested width\&.
-window pathName | Specifies the Tk window managed by the marker\&.
.TE
.SH "OPTION DATABASE"
.PP
Marker options may be supplied through Tk's option database\&. Each concrete marker type has its own resource
class:
.TS
tab(|) box;
l l.
Marker type | Resource class
_
bitmap| BitmapMarker
image| ImageMarker
line| LineMarker
polygon| PolygonMarker
text| TextMarker
window| WindowMarker
.TE
.PP
The resource name is the marker name\&.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
option add *Graph\&.TextMarker\&.Foreground navy
option add *Graph\&.LineMarker\&.LineWidth 2
.fi
.RE

